Storage (Amazon S3): The mobile application requests a secure, temporary link and uploads the raw .mp4 file directly to a cloud bucket.
The Catalyst (AWS Lambda): The exact millisecond the upload finishes, 
an S3 event automatically wakes up a lightweight background function (Lambda). 
This function reads the file's name and location.
The Heavy Lifter (AWS Elemental MediaConvert): The Lambda function doesn't process the video itself. 
It instantly hands a "processing job ticket" to MediaConvert. MediaConvert spins up dedicated virtual processing units,
chops the video into 6-second adaptive bitrate streaming slices (.m3u8 playlist and .ts files),
and saves them into a separate public folder for stutter-free playback in India

Phase 3, Step 2: Creating the Automation Lambda Controller
Now that amplify/storage/resource.ts is ready, it is pointing to a worker script called ./on-upload-handler.ts. We need to physically create that file inside the exact same folder so the system knows what code to execute the millisecond an .mp4 file hits the storage bucket.
Run this command in your active terminal to open the new script file in Vim:

import type { S3Handler } from 'aws-lambda';
import { MediaConvertClient, CreateJobCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-mediaconvert";

// Direct integration into our active Mumbai cluster for rapid execution speeds
const emcClient = new MediaConvertClient({ region: "ap-south-1" });

export const handler: S3Handler = async (event) => {
  const bucket = event.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;
  const key = event.Records[0].s3.object.key;

  // Guardrail Check: Completely skip processing if file lands outside raw-uploads/
  if (!key.startsWith('raw-uploads/')) {
    console.log(`File location ${key} does not require transcoding execution.`);
    return;
  }

  const inputUri = `s3://${bucket}/${key}`;
  // Automatically routes output streaming slices into a clean sub-folder
  const outputUri = `s3://${bucket}/processed-streams/${key.split('/').pop()?.split('.')[0]}/`;

  try {
    const jobCommand = new CreateJobCommand({
      Role: process.env.MEDIACONVERT_ROLE_ARN, // Handled automatically via cross-resource cloud permissions
      Settings: {
        Inputs: [{ FileInput: inputUri }],
        OutputGroups: [{
          Name: "Apple HLS",
          OutputGroupSettings: {
            Type: "HLS_GROUP_SETTINGS",
            HlsGroupSettings: {
              Destination: outputUri,
              SegmentLength: 6, // Enforces strict 6-second slices optimized for Indian mobile networks
              MinSegmentLength: 2
            }
          },
          Outputs: [{ ContainerSettings: { Container: "M3U8" } }]
        }]
      }
    });

    await emcClient.send(jobCommand);
    console.log(`MediaConvert transcode job successfully deployed for asset: ${key}`);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Critical Failure initializing MediaConvert execution pipeline:", error);
    throw error;
  }
};
